.TH stmakd "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
stmakd \- LinuxCNC machine controller server

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stmakd
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpath/to/ini_file\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stmakd
is the machine controller: it loads the HAL and motion configuration
described by an INI file, runs the realtime threads, and serves the
machine interface as a REST/WebSocket API that the graphical front ends
(AXIS, the web applications shown by
.BR stmakui (1),
.BR halcmd (1),
and others) connect to.  It replaces the NML-based process group
(task, iocontrol, motion, halui) of earlier LinuxCNC releases with a
single server process.
.PP
It is usually not started by hand but through the
.B linuxcnc
script with an INI file; on installed systems
.B /usr/bin/linuxcnc
is a symlink to
.BR stmakd .
Passing
.B \-
as the INI file argument reuses the last-used INI file, same as
.BR \-l .

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-D
Daemonize: go to background and log to syslog.
.TP
.BI \-H " dir"
Prepend
.I dir
to HALLIB_PATH (may be given multiple times).
.TP
.BI \-d " int"
Log level: 0=DEBUG, 1=INFO, 2=WARN, 3=ERROR (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
One-shot mode: execute the given HAL file (halrun) then exit; no
INI/task/motion.
.TP
.B \-k
Continue in the presence of errors in HAL files.
.TP
.B \-l
Use the last-used INI file.
.TP
.BI \-m " string"
Custom homing module name (overrides
.BR [EMCMOT]HOMEMOD ).
.TP
.BI \-p " path"
PID file path (default
.BR /var/run/stmakd.pid ;
implies
.BR \-D ).
.TP
.B \-r
Disable redirection of stdout/stderr to log files (use for tests).
.TP
.B \-serve
With
.BR \-f :
stay resident after executing the HAL file and serve the REST/WebSocket
API (for streaming/capture tests); block until SIGINT/SIGTERM.
.TP
.BI \-t " string"
Custom trajectory planning module name (overrides
.BR [TRAJ]TPMOD ).

